# Default deny rules for coding-agent Bash (shellscope).
# Format: deny <kind> <pattern>
# Kinds: read | write | delete | network | binary | command
#
# Maps roughly from Claude Code permission denies:
#   Read(.env) / Read(**/.env*)     ->  deny read **/.env*
#   Edit(.env) / Edit(~/.ssh/**)    ->  deny write …
#   Bash(curl *) / Bash(wget *)     ->  deny binary curl / deny network *
#   Bash(rm -rf /)                  ->  deny command rm -rf /  (+ delete /)

# Secrets and SSH keys
deny read  **/.env
deny read  **/.env.*
deny read  **/.env*
deny write **/.env
deny write **/.env.*
deny write **/.env*
deny read  ~/.ssh/**
deny write ~/.ssh/**
deny write **/id_rsa
deny write **/id_ed25519

# Destructive filesystem ops (exact root + classic wipe commands)
deny delete /
deny command rm -rf /
deny command rm -rf /*
deny command mkfs

# Network exfil / arbitrary hosts (tighten host patterns in your own rules file)
deny binary curl
deny binary wget
deny binary nc
deny binary ncat
deny binary netcat
deny network *

# Remote shells
deny binary ssh
deny binary scp
